# vacti arsenal - CTF (VACTI_CTF_ARSENAL=1)
#
# The apt-installable half of the CTF tool set for kind=ctf engagements. These
# are LIGHTWEIGHT tools from Debian 13 (trixie) main, plus a couple that resolve
# from the pinned Kali apt source (Option A, prio 100) when present. The non-apt
# half (ruby gems, pipx tools, GEF, exploitdb git fallback) is installed by
# golden-image/install-ctf-arsenal.sh, which reads THIS file for its apt step.
#
# Default OFF. Multi-GB / GUI tools (sagemath, ghidra, stegsolve) are NEVER baked
# here; a CTF agent self-heals or the operator installs them deliberately.
#
# One package per line; blank lines and # comments are ignored (same contract as
# web-lean.list / full.list).

# --- Forensics / carving ---
foremost
scalpel
sleuthkit
binwalk

# --- Steganography ---
steghide
libimage-exiftool-perl

# --- Crypto ---
python3-pycryptodome

# --- Pwn / exploitation ---
python3-pwntools
python3-ropgadget
gdb
nasm

# --- Reverse engineering ---
# radare2 is absent from Debian trixie main; it resolves from the pinned Kali
# apt source (Option A). With VACTI_NO_KALI_REPO=1 it is skipped best-effort.
radare2
ltrace
strace

# --- Password cracking ---
john
hashcat

# --- Networking helper ---
netcat-openbsd

# --- Exploit DB / searchsploit ---
# Absent from Debian main; resolves from the pinned Kali source. The installer
# falls back to a git clone of exploit-database when apt cannot supply it.
exploitdb

# --- Toolchain the installer's gem/pipx steps need (idempotent if present) ---
ruby
ruby-dev
python3-pip
